Note on the fix: `WITH SECURITY_ENFORCED` has been deprecated in favor of `WITH USER_MODE`, which is the current recommended syntax for enforcing field- and object-level security (and, as a bonus, sharing rules) on inline SOQL. Behavior here is effectively the same as before — queries run in user mode, respecting the running user's object/field permissions — just expressed with the syntax Salesforce now supports going forward.

